    "extract": "The Cedet, originally known as the Central Department Store, is a modernist building in Warsaw, Poland. Initially built as a department store, it now serves as an office building. It was designed by architects Zbigniew Ihnatowicz and Jerzy Romański, and constructed between 1948 and 1952.",
    "extract_html": "<p>The <b><span><i lang=\"pl\">Cedet</i></span></b>, originally known as the <b>Central Department Store</b>, is a modernist building in Warsaw, Poland. Initially built as a department store, it now serves as an office building. It was designed by architects Zbigniew Ihnatowicz and Jerzy Romański, and constructed between 1948 and 1952.</p>"
